WEBVTT

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.940
What did you just say?

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.150
STRANGE CASE OF
DR. JEKYLL AND MR. HYDE

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.730
H-How would you know about that?

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.360
After all, I...

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.070
- I think I'm gonna bomb that test.
- Me, too.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.290
Excuse me?

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.340
<i>The most horrible incident of my life...</i>

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.550
<i>But let's back up a little before that.</i>

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:34.010
ORESUKI
ARE YOU THE ONLY ONE WHO LOVES ME?

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.600
EPISODE 01
I'M REALLY JUST
AN ORDINARY HIGH SCHOOL STUDENT

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.810
Now this is what I call spring!

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.520
<i>My name is Amatsuyu Kisaragi.</i>

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.520
AMATSUYU KISARAGI (16)
NICKNAME: JORO

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.770
<i>If you take "moon" out of my family name,
you get "Joro."</i>

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.280
JORO

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.280
<i>"Joro," that's my nickname.</i>

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.530
<i>Other than an unusual nickname,
there's nothing remarkable about me.</i>

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.910
<i>I'm an average, run-of-the-mill student.</i>

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.580
Good morning!

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.580
G-Good morning, Himawari.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.670
Stare...

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:08.790
Wh-What?

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:11.090
Yep! You're Joro today, too!

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.340
<i>This is Aoi Hinata.</i>

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.840
AOI HINATA (16)
NICKNAME: HIMAWARI

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.720
<i>You get "Himawari" by mixing up
the characters in her full name, "Aoi Hinata."</i>

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:18.720
HIMAWARI

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.930
<i>She's my cheerful, energetic childhood friend.</i>

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.980
Well, let's go to school together again!

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:31.440
NISHIKIZUTA HIGH SCHOOL

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.400
- Good morning, everyone!
- Good morning!

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.150
Good morning, everyone!

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.030
Good morning!

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.830
Morning, Himawari, Joro!

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:41.660
Good morning!

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:43.580
Hey, you two!

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.120
Sun-chan, good morning!

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.620
Good morning, Sun-chan!

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:49.710
Yeah, good morning!

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.710
<i>This is Sun-chan. His name is Taiyo.
"Sun" is a literal translation.</i>

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:57.840
TAIYO OGA (16)
NICKNAME: SUN-CHAN

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.630
<i>He's the ace of our baseball team,
fourth batter.</i>

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:00.300
<i>Our personalities are opposites,
but, oddly enough, we get along well.</i>

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.560
<i>In fact, Sun-chan has been
my best friend since middle school.</i>

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:07.560
As always, you two are as thick as thieves!

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.020
Right?

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.060
Or an albatross around my neck.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.860
Don't spoil it like that.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.570
That makes me an albatross, too.

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:19.150
I'm happy how things are!
Don't change anything!

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:20.780
R-Right.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.250
What's wrong, Himawari?

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.620
Joro, you're an idiot!

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.580
Hmph!

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.460
What's with her?

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.300
I guess things do change,
whether you like it or not.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.390
What does that mean?

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:45.220
Who knows? Figure it out yourself,
you thick-skulled dork.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.150
LET'S MAKE OUR
DEAREST WISH
COME TRUE AND GO TO
KOSHIEN THIS YEAR!

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:58.860
Well, I'm off to practice!

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.030
You're really into it, huh, Sun-chan?

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.620
Of course! This year,
we're gonna be regional champions,

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.990
then go on to Koshien!

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:08.000
You, too, good luck at student council, Joro!

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:09.330
Thanks!

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.750
- Why?
- What's she doing here?

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.380
Hi, Joro.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.250
President Cosmos!

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.300
Why?

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.970
<i>This is President Cosmos.</i>

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:26.350
SAKURA AKINO (17)
NICKNAME: COSMOS

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:26.350
<i>If you take the "no" out of her real name,
it can be read as "cosmos."</i>

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:30.060
<i>She's the student council president
and a third-year, which is a year ahead of me.</i>

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:35.520
I thought I would pick up
our reliable secretary for a change.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:38.280
Thank you.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:41.740
You go, Joro! Your idol, the president,
gives you door-to-door service.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.070
I'm jealous!

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.780
H-Hey, Sun-chan!

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.330
Thank you.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:51.000
What did you come here for, Cosmos?

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.790
I came to see the person
I wanted to see, Himawari.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.760
Himawari, what's the matter?

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:01.720
Nothing's the matter!

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.390
Well, that's a side benefit.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.850
What does that mean?

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.890
Think about it.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.480
Well, I'm going to practice!

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.860
O-Okay.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:19.320
It seems she doesn't like me.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.740
STUDENT COUNCIL OFFICE

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:23.700
Excuse me.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.950
Well, I'll deliver these to the staff room
on my way out.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:35.040
Um, so, I'll see you on Monday.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:40.340
Joro, do you have a minute?

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.010
What is it?

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.510
U-Um...

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.760
Tomorrow is Saturday,
so would you go somewhere with me?

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.850
Maybe I shouldn't have asked.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:55.770
N-No, it's fine!

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.230
Then tomorrow morning at 10:00.

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:02.400
Why don't we meet up
by the clock tower at the station?

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.740
S-Sure! Of course!

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.110
Great!

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:08.620
That's an okay from you for tomorrow.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:11.200
Well, see you tomorrow!

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.830
Right! See you tomorrow!

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.580
It's a date, right?

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.460
A date with President Cosmos...

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:22.420
From Himawari?

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:24.550
Ah, jeez.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.090
<i>Let's go somewhere tomorrow!</i>

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.510
<i>Sorry. I can't tomorrow.</i>

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:31.220
<i>Then on Sunday! Definitely Sunday!</i>

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.220
<i>Got it?</i>

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:34.930
ALL RIGHT.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:37.310
Guess I can't say no, then.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.900
All right, on to homework.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:47.860
Hi. You're early.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:49.740
G-Good morni—

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.330
Um...

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.540
do I look strange?

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.420
N-No! You're fine!

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.420
Good. Then, let's go.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.460
I-I'm looking forward to it!

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:06.260
Yes, so am I.

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.400
Thank you for lunch.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.610
You went to all the trouble of making it.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.740
It's my way of thanking you
for all your help with student council.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:33.580
Nah, it's nothing.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.040
Um, Joro!

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:38.290
Yes?

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:44.000
A-Actually, I invited you today
because I wanted to tell you something.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:45.710
Tell me something?

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:46.710
Yes!

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.550
Um...

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:57.100
First, would you sit next to me?

00:06:57.470 --> 00:07:00.060
Y-Yes. Sure.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.940
A-Actually, uh...

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.030
there's someone that I like.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.240
O-Okay!

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:15.580
When I think about that person,
my chest feels tight.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:19.960
But just being able to see him every day
is enough to make me happy.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.880
I-I...

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:41.100
I'm in love with your best friend,
Taiyo Oga!

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.480
What?

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:48.860
It all started last year at the final game
of the regional baseball tournament.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.610
L-Last year's final game
of the regional baseball tournament?

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:57.490
As the team's ace, he must've been
more frustrated than anyone at losing.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:04.080
But Oga was encouraging his teammates.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:08.250
Even now, that image of him
is etched in my mind.

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:13.050
But that wasn't his true feeling.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.760
After the game, I was oddly curious,

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.720
so I walked to the players' waiting room
from the east entrance.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:36.950
Oga was crying
while beating his head against the wall.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:41.700
In that moment, I fell in love with him.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:48.210
Unfortunately, I hardly ever
get the chance to talk to him.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.380
And I'm not making any progress.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:56.470
So I know it's pathetic...

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.100
but I want you to help us get together!

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:07.270
M-Maybe it's too much to ask.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.530
Sure. You can count on me.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.540
Thank you! Thank you!

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.870
W-Well...

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.080
See you on Monday.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.550
Oh, no.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:36.010
MEAT WORLD
CHICKEN KINGDOM

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.680
That was great, wasn't it?

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.140
Y-Yeah. Sure was.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:41.260
What's wrong, Joro?

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.520
You haven't been yourself since this morning.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.810
N-No, I'm fine.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:49.020
Oh, right!

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:51.070
In that case...

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:52.980
Himawari power...

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.690
charge up!

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.860
What are you doing?

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.110
Knock it off, Himawari! People are staring!

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:01.950
That perked you right up!

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:11.090
What is it, Joro?

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.250
Nothing. Nothing at all.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:17.470
Thank you, Himawari. You did cheer me up.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.340
Really? All right!

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.860
SUN PARK

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:40.450
How was that?

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:43.240
Sheesh. You're like a little kid.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:45.410
But...

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.710
I had a really good time today.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:50.000
Thank you, Himawari.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:52.840
Me, too.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:56.800
Um, listen, Joro.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:02.470
A-Actually, there's something
I want to tell you.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.390
Something you want to tell me?

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:05.680
That's right!

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:07.930
Um...

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:14.610
First, would you sit next to me?

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:17.570
Y-Yeah. Sure.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:23.160
A-Actually, um...

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.660
there's someone I like.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.500
R-Really?

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:33.710
When I think about him, my chest feels tight.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:38.630
But even just getting to see him
every day makes me happy.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.260
<i>Don't tell me this is...</i>

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.760
I-I...

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:50.020
I'm in love with your best friend, Sun-chan!

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:52.230
Oh, déjà vu.

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:56.900
It all started last year, at the final game
of the regional baseball tournament.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:58.070
<i>The same place for you?</i>

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:03.240
At the time, I'm sure Sun-chan, the team's
ace player, was more frustrated than anyone...

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:04.990
but he was cheering everyone up.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:10.290
Even now, that image of him
is etched in my mind.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:15.080
But I knew the truth! When I was heading
for the waiting room from the west exit...

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.040
<i>West?</i>

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:25.300
Sun-chan was crying
and banging his head against the wall!

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:29.140
That's when I fell in love with him.

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:36.060
But Sun-chan and I have been friends
since middle school, right?

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.400
Yeah.

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:40.480
S-So I think this is pathetic...

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.650
but I want your help!

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:50.580
Y-You won't?

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.670
Sure. Leave it to me.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.130
Thank you! Thank you!

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:06.550
W-Well, see you on Monday!

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:11.850
Oh, my God.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.320
I can't believe this.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.320
Gimme a freakin' break!

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.160
Why is this happening?

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:31.910
I did my best, didn't I?

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:34.500
Didn't I play the obtuse boy to perfection?

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.670
That time, that time, that time,
and that time, I was flawless!

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.130
This is where it ends up?

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:40.590
Don't give me that crap!

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:43.300
Seriously? You love my best friend!
What the hell?

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.630
I know he's cool and the baseball team's ace!

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:47.510
Damn it! Crash and burn!

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.510
I never imagined the romantic comedy
high school plan I'd cooked up

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:52.140
would run into a roadblock like this!

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:55.350
From tomorrow, I might as well
get revenge on them as my true self!

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.730
<i>No, wait.</i>

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:02.070
<i>In this situation,
there are two women and one man.</i>

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:03.980
<i>In other words...</i>

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.820
<i>I have a chance!</i>

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:08.530
Yes! That's it!

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.410
I should do all I can to support them,

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:13.290
while aiming for a happy ending
with whichever one isn't chosen!

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:15.500
My romantic comedy is just getting started!

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:18.120
Just you wait!

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.750
EPISODE 01
I'M REALLY JUST
AN ORDINARY HIGH SCHOOL STUDENT

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.920
EPISODE 01
I'M REALLY JUST
AN ORDINARY BACKGROUND CHARACTER

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.430
Spring can go destroy itself.

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:31.600
<i>My name is Amatsuyu Kisaragi.</i>

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:33.180
AMATSUYU KISARAGI (16)
BACKGROUND CHARACTER

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:33.890
<i>I'm an average,
run-of-the-mill background character.</i>

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:39.190
Good morning!

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.400
G-Good morning, Himawari.

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:44.530
<i>That hurt, damn.</i>

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:46.610
What?

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:48.450
Yep. You're Joro again today!

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:51.660
<i>This is Himawari.</i>

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:52.950
AOI HINATA (16)
NICKNAME: HIMAWARI

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:56.750
<i>She toyed with innocent little me,
exploiting our status as childhood friends.</i>

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.580
CHILDHOOD FRIEND
BITCH

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:57.580
<i>Freakin' bitch.</i>

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:00.120
Thanks for yesterday.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.710
Oh. About that...

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:07.380
On Saturday, President Cosmos
asked me to do the same thing.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.800
So Cosmos really is my rival!

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:14.310
<i>She realized it?</i>

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:18.560
Remember how she suddenly showed up
in our class on Friday?

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:21.980
I had my suspicions,
but I just can't believe this!

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.860
<i>Tell me about it.</i>

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.320
So I'll help both of you.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.030
You're not on my side?

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:29.320
<i>Shut up, you bitch!</i>

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:30.910
I'm on both your sides.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.740
O-Okay.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:36.740
So let's talk about a strategy
for you, Himawari.

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:38.040
You thought of one for me?

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:39.410
Naturally.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.500
Thank you, Joro!

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:49.010
This, and yet she doesn't even like me.
Is that nuts or what?

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:52.220
So, the strategy...

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:54.930
Yo, Joro!

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:56.560
Good morning, Sun-chan!

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:59.390
You didn't come with Himawari today, huh?

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:02.350
It's not like we're always together.

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.980
We're just childhood friends.

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:06.230
I see.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:10.860
Yoo-hoo! I'm gonna join
this conversation all natural-like!

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.240
<i>You're joining it unnaturally!</i>

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:14.700
You wanna get in on this, Himawari?

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.160
Yeah! Let's talk!

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:18.950
<i>Okay, right here.</i>

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:19.950
Sorry!

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:24.540
I have something to do
at the student council office, so you two talk.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.040
<i>That's my line!</i>

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.670
Student Council? You, Himawari?

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:35.180
Oh, that's right! Like Himawari said,

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.260
I have something
at the student council office.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:41.390
Joro! This is my strategy time!
Do your student council stuff later!

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.480
<i>Please, shut up!</i>

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:46.560
A-Anyway, I have to go, so you two talk!

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:48.570
Oh, okay. Gotcha.

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:51.440
Later!

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:53.030
Yeah. Thanks, Joro!

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:55.320
Work hard!

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:57.490
I saw a movie yesterday. With Jo—

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:59.030
- Jo?
- This is...

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:00.740
- Jo-Jokes! Jokes in the movie!
- tough.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:02.960
Have you been waiting long?

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.710
No, sorry for suddenly
asking you to come here.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.630
Don't worry about it, Joro.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.960
<i>This is Cosmos.</i>

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:13.800
SAKURA AKINO (17)
NICKNAME: COSMOS

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:15.550
<i>She used her mature sex appeal
to trifle with my pure heart.</i>

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:17.260
STUDEN COUNCIL PRESIDENT
MINX

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:18.010
<i>The minx!</i>

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:20.010
S-So what did you want to talk about?

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:24.640
Actually, Himawari asked me
the exact same favor that you did.

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:26.100
Himawari!

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:27.650
I knew it.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:30.150
<i>So she realized it, too.</i>

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:33.360
Well, this is a nuisance.

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:34.780
<i>Tell me about it.</i>

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:37.870
So I intend to help both of you.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:41.490
- I thought you were on my side!
- I'm on both your sides.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.830
O-Okay.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:47.670
So let's talk about your strategy,
President Cosmos.

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:49.500
You thought of one for me?

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:50.420
Naturally.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:51.380
Thank you!

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:58.760
<i>It doesn't mean anything when you
grip the hand of a man you don't even like.</i>

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:01.220
So, about your strategy...

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:04.020
H-Hi, Oga.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:06.230
Sorry to make you come all this way.

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:07.060
No prob!

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:10.610
So what'd you wanna talk about,
President Akino?

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:11.770
Well...

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:16.740
<i>Now, use the baseball team budget
as a pretext to be friends.</i>

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.700
I want to be friends!

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:20.950
<i>She blew off the pretext!</i>

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.410
President Akino, you want to be friends?

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.040
<i>Both of you get way ahead of yourselves!</i>

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:31.340
That's perfect, President Cosmos!

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:34.960
As student council president, you should
pay some attention to underclassmen,

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:37.930
and it's a good idea to be Sun-chan's friend.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:40.760
Joro, changing the plan
on the spur of the moment!

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:42.050
What a schemer you are!

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:43.470
<i>Please shut your mouth!</i>

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:45.680
So that's what it is?

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:48.940
Roger that, President Akino... I mean Cosmos!

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:51.610
G-Great!

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:54.230
Thank you, Joro.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:57.700
<i>This is so painful.</i>

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.490
Joro!

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:03.700
Joro!

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.290
Where are you?

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:08.120
Joro!

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:10.040
Joro!

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:12.790
He's not here?

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:16.880
<i>At least during lunch,
I wanna forget all this crap and be free!</i>

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:22.220
About the only quiet place is the school library,
and that's because it isn't open.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:23.550
The only downside...

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.270
Oh. I'm surprised to see you here.

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:29.140
<i>...is that she's always here.</i>

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:33.360
Hello, Sanshokuin.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.900
Hello there.

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:38.690
<i>This is Sumireko Sanshokuin.</i>

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:40.400
SUMIREKO SANSHOKUIN (16)
NICKNAME: PANSY

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:43.240
<i>If you take out three characters
from her name and put them together,</i>

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:45.240
PANSY

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:44.740
<i>you'll get her nickname, "Pansy."</i>

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:49.160
<i>She's the quiet, plain library aide,
but for some reason, only to me...</i>

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.620
I mean, this isn't a pigsty.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:53.830
<i>...she speaks with a really sharp tongue.</i>

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:56.000
Let's talk a bit.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.380
I'd like to just relax.

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.470
I want to talk to you.

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:02.970
Sorry. I'm tired.

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:05.800
Certainly, anyone would be tired
if they had to help their friend

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:08.720
and the president of student council
with romance.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:12.730
What did you just say?

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:17.650
STRANGE CASE OF
DR. JEKYLL AND MR. HYDE

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.270
I guess I have no choice.

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:19.650
Maybe I'll just tell Oga your secret.

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:19.650
BY ROBERT LOUIS STEVENSON
TRANSLATION BY OSHITARO MITAKA

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:23.910
H-How would you know about that?

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:26.990
After all, I've been...

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:30.620
stalking you.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.210
Excuse me?

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:36.380
I've been watching you for a long time.

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:44.220
R-Really? That's one point for you!

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.800
Well, talk to you later.

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:48.970
Maybe I'll tell him all of your secrets.

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:51.270
Let's talk.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:57.270
Wh-Why is that bench here?

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:59.190
Express delivery really is fast.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:01.030
I don't care about how fast they are!

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:04.490
<i>Could this be...</i>

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:08.490
Um, first of all, would you sit next to me?

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:19.250
Actually, there's someone I like.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:21.630
<i>I've got it! It's Sun-chan, right?</i>

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:25.720
Every time I think about him,
there's a tightness in my chest.

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:29.890
But I'm happy
just getting to see him every day.

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:32.810
<i>Sun-chan! Sun-chan!</i>

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:34.230
I...

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>Sun-chan! Sun-chan! Sun-chan!</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:35.480
<i>S-S-S-S-Sun-chan!</i>

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:37.230
<i>Sun-chan! Sun-chan! Sun-chan!</i>

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:38.940
<i>S-S-S-S-Sun-chan!</i>

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:44.740
I'm in love with you, Joro.

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:49.830
<i>Why is this the only classic event?</i>

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:51.660
<i>Of all people, only her?</i>

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:53.120
It all started—

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:55.620
Okay! I've heard enough.

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:57.960
I don't like when you talk like that.

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:02.880
<i>Don't tell me she likes...</i>

00:22:02.510 --> 00:22:06.550
STRANGE CASE OF
DR. JEKYLL AND MR. HYDE

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:06.880
I want to talk to "Hyde."

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:12.600
You mean you like this me?

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:14.730
You must have a screw loose.

00:22:16.440 --> 00:22:17.600
Gross!

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:20.310
Ow!

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:23.190
I have fabled the mean Joro.

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:23.190
SOUVENIRS ENTOMOLOGIQUES
BY JEAN-HENRI FABRE

00:22:23.190 --> 00:22:25.820
That's not the definition
of fables that I know!

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:28.070
My God, I hate you.

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:30.660
Really? I love you.

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:33.200
What do you mean to do with me?

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:38.000
Just so you know,
I would never agree to go out with you.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:40.330
Don't worry. That's not what I have in mind.

00:22:41.630 --> 00:22:44.130
I thought you said
you were in love with me!

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:46.760
Yes, very much so.

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:50.970
I have a favor to ask you.

00:22:50.970 --> 00:22:54.470
- If I don't like it, I can refuse, right?
- You're free to do as you like.

00:22:57.180 --> 00:23:00.900
From now on, I want to talk to you here
every day during lunch.

00:23:00.900 --> 00:23:02.690
- I refuse.
- I refuse your refusal.

00:23:02.690 --> 00:23:04.940
Didn't you say I could choose?

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:10.200
What's the harm? No one would find us here
in this lovely secret spot.

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:13.830
True.

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:15.910
Then it's settled.

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:18.040
Fine.

00:23:19.870 --> 00:23:22.630
<i>Why is this happening?</i>

00:23:22.630 --> 00:23:25.050
<i>After all the effort I put in!</i>

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:27.420
<i>I worked hard to get them to like me!</i>

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:28.260
<i>And yet...</i>

00:23:28.630 --> 00:23:30.720
I'm looking forward
to spending time with you.

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:33.680
<i>...you're the only one who loves me?</i>

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:38.770
<i>I'm attacked by an impossible spiral.</i>
